Not change, but support in a cleaner way.  Right now getters/setters are supported, but you need to make them snake cased as SnakeYAML doesn't support changing that (Jackson does); so the following works today

{code}
private String foo;
private String moreComplex;

public getFoo() { return foo; }
public setFoo(String v) { foo = v; }

// ugly
public getMore_complex() { return moreComplex; }
public setMore_complex(String v) { moreComplex = v;}
{code}

One concern that gets brought up is that setter validation gets duplicated as we can't block in 1 consistent way, by fixing the getter/setter camel -> snake case thing, we can avoid this problem when we feel its best to.

